{"homeWinPercentage":0.9767,"playId":"401869963302","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9761,"playId":"401869963306","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9749,"playId":"401869963311","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9757,"playId":"401869963316","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9766,"playId":"401869963322","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.978,"playId":"401869963326","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9792,"playId":"401869963329","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9799,"playId":"401869963332","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9787,"playId":"401869963337","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9764,"playId":"401869963343","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9765,"playId":"401869963352","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.978,"playId":"401869963356","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9739,"playId":"401869963360","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9721,"playId":"401869963366","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9736,"playId":"401869963370","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3651","guid":"7cc50a9f-aab4-3045-beec-707069d1b0e4","fullName":"Bridgeforth Stadium","address":{"city":"Harrisonburg","state":"VA","zipCode":"22807","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[]},"attendance":25005},"article":{"headline":"Hayden Wolfe's field goal in OT lifts Troy to 24-21 victory over James Madison","description":"— Hayden Wolfe kicked a 27-yard field goal in overtime and Troy rallied from a 14-point deficit to beat James Madison 24-21 on Thursday night.","story":"HARRISONBURG, Va. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5388767/hayden-wolfe\" target=\"_new\">Hayden Wolfe</a> kicked a 27-yard field goal in overtime and Troy rallied from a 14-point deficit to beat James Madison 24-21 on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              Troy (4-4, 2-2 Sun Belt Conference) turned the ball over on downs at the Dukes' 41-yard line to start the game, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5153978/camden-coleman\" target=\"_new\">Camden Coleman</a> tossed a 2-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5165803/corey-scott\" target=\"_new\">Corey Scott</a> on fourth-and-goal nine plays later for a 7-0 lead.\n\n\r\n              Coleman fired a 31-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5078227/braeden-wisloski\" target=\"_new\">Braeden Wisloski</a> and James Madison (7-2, 4-2) led 14-0 after its first two possessions.\n\n\r\n              The Trojans cut it to 14-7 when <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5388754/gavin-griffin\" target=\"_new\">Gavin Griffin</a> ran it in from a yard out on the first play of the second quarter. Troy picked up three first downs on James Madison penalties to extend the drive.\n\n\r\n              The Dukes answered with a third straight touchdown drive, scoring on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5225435/seth-cromwell\" target=\"_new\">Seth Cromwell</a>'s 14-yard run for a 21-7 advantage at halftime.\n\n\r\n              Justin <a href=\"https://x.com/TroyTrojansFB/status/2115983102392840671?a=--6Hp5iaGcNmh--uYoXQ&s=20\">Powe intercepted a pass</a> by Dukes backup <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5172036/jc-evans\" target=\"_new\">JC Evans</a> two plays into the third quarter and returned it 37 yards for a touchdown to get the Trojans within seven. Powe picked off three passes to tie Ronnie Shelley's single-game school record set in 1968.\n\n\r\n              JMU followed its three scoring drives with four three-and-outs and five turnovers on its next nine possessions.\n\n\r\n              Troy turned the fourth turnover — a fumble recovery — into a 28-yard touchdown run by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5086097/jaheim-merriweather\" target=\"_new\">Jaheim Merriweather</a> three plays later to tie it 21-all heading to the fourth quarter.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4912119/tucker-kilcrease\" target=\"_new\">Tucker Kilcrease</a> completed 15 of 31 passes for 179 yards for the Trojans, who improved to 1/3 on the road. Merriweather totaled 84 yards on 13 rushes.\n\n\r\n              Coleman had 175 yards on 14-for-25 passing for the Dukes with two interceptions. Cromwell finished with 135 yards on 23 rushes.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Troy: Hosts Louisiana Tech on Nov. 7.\n\n\r\n              James Madison: At Southern Mississippi on Nov. 5.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://na01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Fnewsletters&data=05%7C02%7C%7Cdcd4c927a3014947713f08def3da887f%7C84df9e7fe9f640afb435aaaaaaaaaaaa%7C1%7C0%7C639216317087773713%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=592GG7Tx9gHi6vEFt3ytKh9NsJsnsJX5%2FPfFbPmAML8%3D&reserved=0\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://na01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Fhub%2Fap-top-25-college-football-poll&data=05%7C02%7C%7Cdcd4c927a3014947713f08def3da887f%7C84df9e7fe9f640afb435aaaaaaaaaaaa%7C1%7C0%7C639216317087791086%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=ia6nZ9tg%2FZcgm%2BFi8LWTUGjusXBzP7sDOqfdsmjeNig%3D&reserved=0\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://na01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Fhub%2Fcollege-football&data=05%7C02%7C%7Cdcd4c927a3014947713f08def3da887f%7C84df9e7fe9f640afb435aaaaaaaaaaaa%7C1%7C0%7C639216317087810304%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=qcVbI2ec6BmMJKNCLT%2FCF